BIOMOLECULE: 1
THIS ENTRY CONTAINS THE CRYSTALLOGRAPHIC ASYMMETRIC UNIT
WHICH CONSISTS OF 1 CHAIN(S). SOME REPORTS INDICATE
THAT THE BIOLOGICAL UNIT FOR THE PROTEIN IS A DIMER.
HOWEVER, THE TRUNCATED BACE IS FULLY FUNCTIONAL AS A
MONOMER IN SOLUTION.
